rl":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/deployments","created_at":"2012-09-06T00:04:56Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T01:23:29Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-08T14:21:53Z","git_url":"git://github.com/g-truc/glm.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:g-truc/glm.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/g-truc/glm.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/g-truc/glm","homepage":"https://glm.g-truc.net","size":74759,"stargazers_count":10499,"watchers_count":10499,"language":"C++","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":2317,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":108,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["cpp","cpp-library","glm","header-only","mathematics","matrix","opengl","quaternion","simd","sycl","vector","vulkan"],"visibility":"public","forks":2317,"open_issues":108,"watchers":10499,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"Prior to the introduction of the initalizer-list constructors, this code creates an identity quaternion:\n\n```\nglm::quat{1.0f, 0.0f, 0.0f, 0.0f}\n```\n\nAfter the introduction of the initializer-list constructors, the same code creates a _different quaternion_ (setting x=1 and w=0, whereas before it set w=1, x=0). This does not result in any compile time error or warning, because the code is still correct, it just results in a bug at runtime.\n\nPrior to the introduction of the initializer-list constructors, this code creates an identity matrix:\n\n```\nglm::mat4{1.0f}\n```\n\nAfter the introduction of the initializer-list constructors, the same code compiles but causes an assertion failure at runtime.\n\nThis seems to me to be a step backwards in usability, introducing ambiguity and reducing the effectiveness of compiler type checking in confirming that the API is being used correctly. Note that the uniform initialization syntax is recommended by people such as Herb Sutter for general use (see, [Elements of Modern C++ Style](http://herbsutter.com/elements-of-modern-c-style/)); ie, it is not strange to use it by default in C++11 (it's not intended only for initializer lists).\n\nIf you guess that I'm writing this issue because I've just been stung by these problems, you are correct.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/issues/159/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/issues/159/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":91903250,"node_id":"MDE1OlJlZmVyZW5jZWRFdmVudDkxOTAzMjUw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/issues/events/91903250","actor":{"login":"Groovounet","id":367227,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NzIyNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/367227?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet","html_url":"https://github.com/Groovounet","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.c